---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../config";

const email = site.contactEmail;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use"
  description={`The plain-language terms for using ${site.name}. Tools are free, provided as-is, and you must own the files you process.`}
  canonicalPath="/terms"
>
  <div class="page">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="page__intro">
        <p class="micro">Terms</p>
        <h1>Terms of use</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Plain-language rules for using this site. By using a tool, you agree
          to these terms.
        </p>
        <p class="tool-note">Last updated: 24 November 2026</p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          “We” means {site.name}, operated by {site.maker} in {site.location}.
          You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Free tools, as they are</h2>
        <p>
          The tools are provided free of charge, “as is” and “as available”. We
          work to keep them accurate and reliable, but we cannot promise that
          every file will work, that a result will be perfect, or that the site
          will always be online.
        </p>

        <h2>Your files and your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You are responsible for the files you open. Only process files you
          own or have permission to use. Do not use the tools to break copyright
          law, privacy law or any other law that applies to you.
        </p>
        <p>
          The tools convert only files you select from your own device. They do
          not download content from YouTube, TikTok or any other platform, and
          they must not be used for that purpose.
        </p>

        <h2>Keep your own copy</h2>
        <p>
          Always keep the original file. Processing can remove information
          permanently — for example, metadata cannot be restored after it is
          stripped. We cannot recover a file for you because we never receive
          it.
        </p>

        <h2>No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          To the extent allowed by law, we make no warranties about the tools,
          including fitness for a particular purpose or freedom from errors.
          Some jurisdictions do not allow certain warranty exclusions, so part
          of this section may not apply to you.
        </p>

        <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the extent allowed by law, we are not liable for indirect or
          consequential losses, lost data, lost profits or damage arising from
          your use of the site. This does not limit liability that cannot be
          limited by law.
        </p>

        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Do not attack, overload or attempt to break the site.</li>
          <li>Do not use the tools for illegal or harmful activity.</li>
          <li>Do not remove copyright notices from other people's work.</li>
          <li>
            Do not use automated requests in a way that harms the service for
            other people.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          © {new Date().getFullYear()} {site.name}. All rights reserved. This
          applies to the site's own design, text and code. Open-source
          libraries used by the tools remain under their own licences. Brand
          names mentioned on the site belong to their owners.
        </p>

        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          The site relies on hosting, code delivery and possibly analytics or
          advertising services from third parties. Their own terms and privacy
          policies apply to those services.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of {site.location}.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          These terms may be updated as the site changes. The date at the top of
          the page will show the latest version. Continued use after a change
          means you accept the updated terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms can be sent to{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
